00:06:55.920 --> 00:07:01.840
Something I can’t put in the description&nbsp;
below, is describe how much I love that scene.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:15.920
I mean. What a rollercoaster of a chapter. So much&nbsp;
negativity, cruelty and immorality building up in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:23.200
just 16 pages. Emotional storytelling at its&nbsp;
best. I think you will probably already have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:30.800
a good idea what makes this chapter so incredibly&nbsp;
dark, even though no-one dies, no-one is betrayed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:38.240
and nothing is lost. I think Kid summaries it best&nbsp;
in this panel here, where he fittingly describes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:49.040
the auction house as a miniature of the world.&nbsp;
What does he mean by that? Well you see, Sabaody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:55.760
is the first arc that we actually meet the world&nbsp;
nobles and see their rule and tyranny in action.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.480 --> 00:08:02.800
In the world of One Piece they stand on top of&nbsp;
the food chain. They are a tiny group of people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:09.520
that hold most of the wealth and power of the&nbsp;
world. Anything that they want, they get. Laws&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:15.920
don’t apply to them, they are made to make their&nbsp;
lives better. They have complete control over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:21.200
the World Government and if a civilian so much&nbsp;
as crosses paths with one without bowing down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:28.880
they will be shot and killed. They literally see&nbsp;
themselves as the gods of the One Piece world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:34.800
and they certainly behave and live that way.&nbsp;
And so when Kid says that the slave auction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:40.480
is like the world in miniature it tells us an&nbsp;
awful lot about the state of the world itself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:46.720
As will be confirmed later in the story,&nbsp;
it means that even on a large scale, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:53.840
Celestial Dragons simply do what they want with a&nbsp;
disregard for human life, morality and humanity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:06.720
They dominate everything and everyone and no-one&nbsp;
is able to lift so much as a finger against them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:13.280
Luffy’s friend Camie suddenly is nothing more&nbsp;
than a product that is sold to the highest bidder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:20.160
to amuse his twisted fantasies. So the scene&nbsp;
gives us a first major glimpse at who the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:25.920
World Government truly represents and what the&nbsp;
true cruelty of the One Piece world looks like.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:32.800
And, just as Kid stated the Human auction House&nbsp;
is a wonderful narrative symbol for all of that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:39.440
Even though it is the centre of unjust and inhuman&nbsp;
slave trade, the Marines euphemistically refer to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:46.080
it as the Public Employment Security Office. I&nbsp;
probably don’t have to tell you that referring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:51.680
to slave work as employment has happened plenty&nbsp;
of times throughout real history as well in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:59.200
attempt to soften and normalise the exploitation&nbsp;
of humans. It’s not a mere sign of corruption&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:05.040
within the marines, but they literally have&nbsp;
no other choice but to look the other way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:11.920
as they directly obey the celestial dragons’ rule.&nbsp;
What makes the symbolism of the auction house even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:17.520
more fitting however is the fact that it was&nbsp;
owned by none other than Donquixote Doflamingo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:23.600
the leader of the Underworld, powerful warlord&nbsp;
and one of the cruelest antagonists in the story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:35.840
It truly says nothing good about the world&nbsp;
if it resembles something run by Doflamingo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:40.320
who’s own country that can also be&nbsp;
seen as a miniature of the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:44.800
was one of the darkest and corrupt&nbsp;
places the straw hats have visited.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:50.800
Doflamingo being a former Celestial Dragon himself&nbsp;
is of course just the the cherry on top then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:59.840
as he himself has suffered his entire&nbsp;
life under the system of the world nobles.

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:09.920
And so thematically this darkest of chapters&nbsp;
fits more than perfectly into the arguably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:15.440
darkest arc of the series so far. All this&nbsp;
stuff with nobles, people being bought and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:21.040
sold and walked around with collars, people&nbsp;
being sold like items in an auction house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:26.160
Hachi and Camie having to hide themselves&nbsp;
due to long-standing racism that's still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:32.720
heavily ingrained in the people of the world.&nbsp;
And that is only the first part of the arc.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:38.320
It leaves a quite disturbing and uncomfortable&nbsp;
feel on us readers, as we were mostly used to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:44.400
more adventure-based story-line with smaller&nbsp;
villains in between. Yet here the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:51.200
political system of the world is revealed to be&nbsp;
twisted and broken, designed for the pleasure of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:58.160
a selected few and exploiting the rest. Kid, who&nbsp;
I think got a wonderful introduction in this arc,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:02.320
has a fantastic and incredibly&nbsp;
underrated speech about all this. I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:16.240
this hits it on the head. As Kid states&nbsp;
correctly, many pirates like himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:22.640
have done horrendous things. However they are&nbsp;
not a unified group like the world government.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:28.480
And it was the terror, injustice and poverty&nbsp;
of the current system that lead to the high&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:37.840
level of piracy in the first place, Luffy’s&nbsp;
backstory being a great example of this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:45.440
And so I would argue that Oda&nbsp;
tries to make clear in this chapter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:50.720
that the world government is overall the&nbsp;
greater evil compared to the pirates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:56.320
which is also why true change has come by&nbsp;
the hands of pirates such as Roger and Luffy.

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:06.000
So let’s finally talk about that punch, that&nbsp;
I think we all immensely enjoyed seeing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:12.640
It’s especially nicely done in the anime where&nbsp;
the change from black to white, Luffy’s walk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:19.440
Charlos’ dropping face as well as the unique&nbsp;
sound design really bring the scene to life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:25.600
and multiply its impact. Based on everything we&nbsp;
have discussed so far, I think it’s very easy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:34.560
to see what makes Luffy’s moment of pure anger&nbsp;
so cathartic. Luffy is the only one who dares&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:40.960
to stand up to the true injustice and tyranny&nbsp;
of the world, who actually shows Charlos you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:47.520
can’t just do whatever to people and that actions&nbsp;
actually should have consequences, something that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:55.520
no admiral, no yonko and no one else has dared&nbsp;
to do. In that sense, when Luffy punches Charlos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.520 --> 00:14:01.040
and bursts the bubble that is supposed to keep him&nbsp;
from breathing the same air as the common people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:08.240
Luffy also bursts his metaphoric bubble of&nbsp;
divine and unlimited power. Once again the D&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:16.000
as the natural enemy of the gods. Luffy committing&nbsp;
the ultimate sin and declaring war on the gods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:24.080
themselves. Thus, what makes this scene so special&nbsp;
is that it is a moral and emotional island of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:32.880
light in a see of darkness that is the sabaody&nbsp;
arc. Luffy giving us this moment of much needed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:38.320
justice and courage that allows us to hope for&nbsp;
the world to truly change for the better with him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:45.520
Which is EXACTLY what so many other people&nbsp;
see in him. When the pirate captain bites&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:57.840
off his tongue earlier in the chapter to escape&nbsp;
slavery, Sanji in a great moment comments this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:06.320
It’s all about freedom. And his captan in&nbsp;
this scene is once again proving that he is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:12.640
the freest of them all, free to actually do&nbsp;
the right thing and stand up to the world.&nbsp;

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:23.120
What ultimately makes this&nbsp;
moment even better for me however&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:32.080
is how in typical shakespearean fashion it is&nbsp;
the catalyst for even more tragedy to happen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:38.800
Luffy bravely punching Carlos leads to the&nbsp;
eviction of a Buster Call, during which Kizaru&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:46.480
and Shutenmaru completely overwhelm the crew as&nbsp;
well as the other supernova. In the end Luffy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:52.800
us readers had to witness how one by one each of&nbsp;
the straw hats disappears by the hands of Kuma,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.800 --> 00:16:00.480
resulting in maybe THE most shocking moment of&nbsp;
the entire story. The straw hat’s full defeat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:08.800
All, set up by this moment right here. This is&nbsp;
story telling and tragic writing at its peak.

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:13.680
And speaking of tragic writing at&nbsp;
its peak in the next video I want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:21.840
to talk about one of the most tragic and&nbsp;
misunderstood moments after the time skip.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:33.760
And so we’ll be looking at that in&nbsp;
the next video. Thanks guys. Peace.

